        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 72-year-old male patient, admitted on 12/12/2021 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, clinical examination revealed markedly reduced air entry with expiratory wheeze, increased work of breathing, and oxygen saturation of 84% on room air. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated hypercapnic respiratory failure. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, controlled oxygen therapy, and closely monitored with pulse oximetry and regular vital signs. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Spirometry and patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management were provided prior to discharge. Please ensure close follow-up and review of his maintenance inhaler regimen.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
